			<div id="fsPageBody" class="fsStyleAutoclear fsPageBody">

				<main id="fsPageContent" class="fsPageContent">




							<div class="fsPageLayout fsLayout fsOneColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_16227" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_16228"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_20830" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<center><figure class="fsImage"><a href="#"><picture><img alt="The text %22Board of Education%22 in red and black is positioned on the left, while the logo for the School District of South Orange &amp;amp; Maplewood is on the right, all set against a plain white background." data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v1752058071/somsdk12njus/laggsix5ox2xmxvfh8nc/25-07-09-boe-webheader.svg%22,%22width%22:818}]" data-resource-description="" data-resource-filename="25-07-09-boe-webheader.svg" data-resource-uuid="23b1f0c0-18ba-4cb0-9b78-dbc9f1962a0c" loading="lazy" src="" style="" width="90%"></picture></a></figure></center>


	</div>


	</div>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsLayout fsTwoColumnWideLeftLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_20824" data-use-new="true" >

						<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleTwoThirds fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-1 fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_20825"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_23452" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<h2>Responsibilities of the School Board</h2>

<p>The South Orange &amp; Maplewood School District is guided by a dedicated Board of Education, made up of nine community members elected by voters in South Orange Village&nbsp;and Maplewood Township. These individuals bring their passion and perspective to three-year terms, with elections held each year to welcome new or returning members. Together, they shape the future of our schools through thoughtful policymaking and stewardship.</p>

<p>In addition to setting district policy, the Board selects the Superintendent, approves staff appointments and transitions, and helps ensure our schools have the resources and programs needed for students to thrive. The Board of Education also approves the district&rsquo;s budget, while the tax levy is reviewed separately by the <a href="/board/bose" style="color: #ba0c2f; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline dotted #A2AAAD; text-decoration-thickness: 0.1rem;" target="_blank">Board of School Estimate</a>. This collaborative group includes members from both municipalities and representatives from the School Board.</p>

<p>Each January, the Board holds its annual reorganization meeting to elect a President and two Vice Presidents and to establish its committees.&nbsp;These committees meet monthly to explore important topics and recommend actions that support district goals.</p>


	</div>


	</div>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_23453" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<h2>Board Meetings</h2>

<p style="margin-bottom: -40px;">The Board of Education meets on the third Monday of each month, except when precluded by a holiday. The Board, from time to time, will add additional meetings. Public sessions of all meetings of the Board are held at the Board Administration building, located at 525 Academy Street in Maplewood, and convene at 7:30 PM.</p>


	</div>


	</div>
	
